NAME
    clear - clear the terminal screen

SYNOPSIS
    clear

DESCRIPTION
    Clears the terminal screen and scrollback buffer by writing the ANSI
    escape sequence ESC[H ESC[2J ESC[3J when standard output is attached
    to an interactive terminal. When standard output is not a terminal
    (such as a pipe, redirection, sourced script, or non-interactive
    console), clear does nothing and succeeds.

    A host frontend may override clear with its own implementation to
    clear an embedded console view.

EXAMPLES
    clear

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    dianash(1), echo(1)
